Building
--------

The host platform is detected automatically, or it can be selected explicitly:

    make PLATFORM=linux
    make PLATFORM=macos
    make PLATFORM=sgi

macOS uses the native Metal backend and does not require OpenGL or XQuartz.
Linux and the historical Unix targets keep the X11/GLX backend. Build products
are written to build/<platform>-<graphics>-<audio>/ so configurations do
not reuse incompatible object files.

IRIX 6.x uses the installed SGI `make` and MIPSpro `cc` directly. The normal
command builds strict ANSI C89 with OpenGL and the native SGI stereo audio
backend. Use `AUDIO=none` for a silent build. macOS uses CoreAudio, Linux uses
OSS, and Solaris/SunOS use `/dev/audio`. All native backends share the
same positional stereo mixer described in `docs/audio.md`.
Spatial gain smoothing is enabled by default. Pass `AUDIO_SMOOTHING=0` while
building, or `--no-audio-smoothing` while running, to reduce mixer work on an
older machine without disabling sound.

Game content is external and required at runtime. The `assets/manifest.txt`
file declares models, textures, animation clips, and auxiliary files. Stable
engine render slots are mapped to those replaceable catalog entries by
`assets/config/render.bindings`. Models are Khronos glTF 2.0 binary files under
`assets/models`; textures are under `assets/textures`. The normal game build
does not compile the old C model factories as a fallback.

Battlefields are versioned JSON packages under `assets/maps`. The old split
`road/tree/tank.data` representation and its fallback loader have been removed;
`map.json` is the only runtime and source format on every platform.

Run `make help` to see all supported values. Run the game with `--map 0`,
`--map Andyville`, or another entry shown by `-help` to select one of the
existing external battlefields. See `assets/readme.md` and
`docs/assets-and-maps.md` for the asset format and compatibility policy. See
`docs/content-authoring.md` for the complete guide to static and animated GLB
models, gameplay entities, creatures, NPCs, vehicles, effects, perception,
reactions, triggers, and map actors. The
checked-in GLB files are now the source assets; the removed C geometry
factories and primitive model generator are no longer part of the build or
repository.
